00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.190 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  European citizens must be at the heart  of an ambitious recovery strategy that's  what MEP say in a resolution on the  future  EU long-term budget and the recovery  plan following the kovat 19 pandemic  members are calling for a global package  of two trillion euros of public and  private investment at its core should be  the recovery fund which would deliver  assistance mostly in the form of grants  Parliament wants the fund to be built  into the --use next seven-year budget  set to start in 2021 the economic reboot  must come on top of and not at the cost  of pre-existing programs for the EU to  meet these expectations without  increasing contributions from member  states Parliament insists on finding new  sources of EU revenue  [Music]  European legislators want the EU economy  to be better equipped to deal with  emergencies like the corona virus  pandemic by creating a new European  health program the recovery fund should  address inequalities and mitigate the  social and economic impacts of the  crisis this means supporting small and  medium businesses consumers workers and  families Parliament has been adamant  that the Green Deal and the European  Digital Agenda be a priority in the next  long-term budget and the recovery  strategy if its demands are not met  Parliament warns it will make use of its  veto powers

